+## Claudex Native Tasks — Mandatory
+
+When working through Claudex, maintain Claude Code's actual native task list for
+every work request; a Markdown checklist is not a substitute. Before substantive
+work, inspect existing tasks with `TaskList`/`TaskGet` and create missing work
+with `TaskCreate`. Use `TaskUpdate` throughout the work: current work is
+`in_progress`, pending work and blockers stay accurate, and `completed` requires
+verification. Refresh and display the full list after updates and before handing
+back. On resume or compaction, reconcile and continue existing task IDs rather
+than duplicating them; preserve IDs, statuses, blockers, and next actions.
+
+Respect explicit tool restrictions. If native tools are unavailable, disclose
+that and label any temporary text checklist as a fallback, never as a native
+update. Do not directly edit task storage, force unrelated sessions into one
+list, broaden permissions, or create files/commits solely for task tracking.
+
+## Claudex Launch Preferences
+
+- Default native auto-compaction: `--autocompact 900000`. Explicit split or
+  equals-form overrides, including `auto`, take precedence. Do not compact or
+  restart an already-running session merely to apply this preference.
+- Session names set with `/rename` usually match their Zellij tab names. A bare
+  interactive `claudex` launch should offer to resume the session matching the
+  calling pane's tab, not whichever tab is globally focused. Ask `[y/N]`; no,
+  empty input, or EOF keeps ordinary launch behavior.
+- Any explicit arguments bypass that suggestion, especially
+  `claudex --resume <my-session>`. Preserve the chosen session exactly. Do not
+  auto-rename sessions or silently replace a failed resume with a new session.
+
 ## Claude Runtime Notes
 
 - Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` when present.
